& [DependencyFinding] is no new package but a new direct contract
  + [Cargo_lock] already contains windows-sys 0.61.2 and windows-link 0.2.1
  + [transitive_origin] is mio and tokio
  + [resolved_features] already include Win32_Foundation, Win32_Security, and Win32_Storage_FileSystem
  + [proposed_direct_dependency] is target cfg(windows), exact compatible 0.61.2, default-features false, and those three feature groups
  + [why_Security] CreateFileW is generated only when Win32_Security is enabled because its signature names SECURITY_ATTRIBUTES
  + [expected_lock_delta] is none, subject to an exact clean-copy Cargo proof
  - never: rely on another dependency to keep Cantor's required feature set activated

& [PlatformProposal] is deliberately narrow
  + [minimum_API] is Windows 8 because FileIdInfo is not supported before Windows 8 and Windows Server 2012
  + [initial_execution_target] is the current x86_64 Windows desktop host on a disposable local NTFS fixture
  + [ReFS] has the required 128-bit identity form but must not be claimed supported until stream, link, sparse, and reconstruction fixtures pass there
  + [remote_filesystem] is unsupported in profile 0.1
  + [other_Windows_filesystem] is unsupported until separately classified

& [CallSet] is smaller than the first sketch
  + [CreateFileW] opens one terminal entry without reparse processing
  + [GetFileInformationByHandleEx_FileAttributeTagInfo] returns attributes and diagnostic reparse tag
  + [GetFileInformationByHandleEx_FileIdInfo] returns volume serial and 128-bit file ID
  + [GetFileInformationByHandleEx_FileStandardInfo] returns link count, length, delete-pending, and directory facts
  + [GetFileInformationByHandleEx_FileStreamInfo] returns all stream records on the same handle
  + [GetLastError] captures a failing call's numeric error immediately
  + [OwnedHandle_from_raw_handle] transfers successful raw-handle ownership exactly once
  + [File_from_OwnedHandle] safely converts a regular-file handle for bounded standard Read
  - never: call GetFileInformationByHandle, FindFirstStreamW, FindNextStreamW, FindClose, ReadFile, CloseHandle, DeviceIoControl, privilege APIs, or any mutating API in profile 0.1

& [CreateFileWInvariant] is exact
  + [path_buffer] is owned UTF-16, NUL-terminated, interior-NUL-free, and alive for the call
  + [regular_access] is FILE_GENERIC_READ
  + [directory_access] is FILE_READ_ATTRIBUTES
  + [share] is FILE_SHARE_READ plus FILE_SHARE_WRITE plus FILE_SHARE_DELETE so observation does not masquerade as an exclusion lock
  + [creation] is OPEN_EXISTING
  + [flags] are FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT plus FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS
  + [security_attributes] is null
  + [template] is null
  + [failure] is INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE followed immediately by GetLastError
  + [success] transfers the handle immediately into one OwnedHandle
  - never: retain two owners, construct ownership from INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE, request write/delete access, or omit no-follow

& [FixedOutputInvariant] applies to AttributeTagInfo, IdInfo, and StandardInfo
  + [handle] is borrowed from a live OwnedHandle or File
  + [buffer] is correctly aligned MaybeUninit of the exact generated structure
  + [size] is size_of of that structure converted without truncation to u32
  + [class] and [structure] are a closed exact pair
  + [success] is the only branch that may assume initialization
  + [failure] captures GetLastError before any other FFI call
  + [cross_check] directory, length, attributes, reparse, and link facts must reconcile with the higher-level entry kind

& [VariableStreamInvariant] is checked-record parsing
  + [buffer] is 8-byte aligned and bounded before the call
  + [call] is GetFileInformationByHandleEx with FileStreamInfo on the same owned entry
  + [record_header] must fit before any field is read
  + [NextEntryOffset] is zero for the last record or nonzero, 8-byte aligned, forward-moving, and within initialized bytes
  + [StreamNameLength] is even, within the current record, and within the path/stream policy bound
  + [StreamSize] and [StreamAllocationSize] must be nonnegative
  + [UTF16] must decode without replacement
  + [names] are copied into owned strings before the buffer is released
  + [count] and [aggregate_bytes] are hard bounded
  + [no_stream] preserves ERROR_HANDLE_EOF distinctly
  + [unsupported_or_insufficient] remains a typed failure until exact target-host behavior is proven
  - never: cast an unaligned Vec<u8> pointer to FILE_STREAM_INFO, trust an unchecked offset, or let a reference escape the backing buffer

& [StreamBufferDecision] avoids partial-result ambiguity
  + [protocol_evidence] Microsoft specifies STATUS_BUFFER_OVERFLOW can return only complete records when the output buffer fills
  + [allocation] is one preallocated 4194304-byte 8-aligned buffer, subject to checked u32 conversion
  + [attempts] is exactly one FileStreamInfo call per observation
  + [success] parses the complete chain and requires a terminal zero NextEntryOffset
  + [failure] ignores every buffer byte, captures the numeric error, and rejects as unsupported_or_resource_limited
  + [partial] is never interpreted as complete stream evidence
  + [reason] is a bounded single attempt is simpler and more honest than depending on undocumented Win32 required-size reporting

& [ReadInvariant] uses safe standard I/O after one ownership transfer
  + [conversion] File from OwnedHandle is stable and consumes the OwnedHandle
  + [read] uses a fixed reusable buffer and checked cumulative byte count
  + [limit] stops before exceeding maximum_file_bytes or maximum_total_bytes
  + [EOF] is required exactly at the declared content length
  + [post_read] repeats same-handle attribute, identity, standard, and stream observations
  + [drop] File closes the handle through standard RAII
  - never: reopen by path for content, create a second owning wrapper, memory-map content, or read after a mismatched pre-observation

& [UnsafeBudget] is auditable
  + [call_sites] are CreateFileW, four GetFileInformationByHandleEx classes, immediate GetLastError branches, and one OwnedHandle from_raw_handle transfer
  + [wrapper] exposes safe owned results and typed errors only
  + [module_policy] is deny unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn and document every unsafe block
  + [test_policy] is malformed-buffer parsing is tested as pure byte logic without FFI
  + [non_Windows] compiles an explicit unsupported adapter with no windows-sys import

& [VolumeAndRemotePreflight] is required but not yet in the admitted call set
  + [FileRemoteProtocolInfo] can return FILE_REMOTE_PROTOCOL_INFO from the same root handle and is the candidate remote-protocol observation
  + [GetVolumeInformationByHandleW] can return filesystem name, volume serial, maximum component length, and capability flags from the same root handle
  + [volume_flags] include named streams, hard links, sparse files, reparse points, persistent ACLs, and open-by-file-ID support
  + [SMB_boundary] Microsoft documents GetVolumeInformationByHandleW as unsupported for SMB 3.0, while FileRemoteProtocolInfo is explicitly a remote-protocol structure
  + [initial_policy] requires a successful local NTFS volume observation and an explicit no-remote result
  + [open_question] exact local-handle FileRemoteProtocolInfo success or failure semantics must be measured before its error is classified
  + [authority] is API candidate research only

& [UnresolvedBeforeActivation] is blocking
  + [stream_buffer_behavior] the single-attempt success and bounded-failure policy must be confirmed on the target OS; no error-specific resize behavior is required
  + [share_policy] read-write-delete sharing versus a narrower quiescence-enforcing share mask needs an explicit threat-model decision
  + [attributes] exact admitted and rejected bit masks remain to be frozen
  + [delete_pending] must always reject and quarantine classification must be fixed
  + [root_path] extended-length, UNC, volume, device, reserved-name, case, and trailing-component rules remain to be frozen
  + [filesystem] volume filesystem-name observation and local-versus-remote proof API remain to be selected
  + [dependency] clean-copy Cargo feature and lock diff remains unexecuted

& [AuthorityEffect] is none
  + [next_step] is preserve a separately selected M2B activation source only after unresolved items are closed
  - never: cite this review as permission to edit Cargo.toml, add unsafe, call Win32, create fixtures, inspect a candidate, launch a writable sandbox, mutate, seal, clean, or promote
